46","name":"Rep. Edwards, Chuck","party":"R","state":"NC"},"stage":"on_calendar","stage_label":"On a chamber calendar","summary":"The Equal Representation Act of 2025 changes how the decennial census gathers information and how U.S. House of Representatives seats and electoral votes are distributed among states. It requires the census to collect citizenship status for all household members, mandates that the statement sent to Congress for apportioning representatives exclude noncitizens, and requires public reporting of these statistics.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"Will be counted as the sole basis for the apportionment of U.S. Representatives and electoral votes beginning with the 2030 census.","group":"U.S. Citizens"},{"effect":"Will be required to report their citizenship status on census questionnaires and will be excluded from the population totals used for Congressional apportionment.","group":"Noncitizens"},{"effect":"Will have their number of U.S. Representatives and electoral votes determined using only the count of U.S. citizens rather than all persons.","group":"States"}],"key_provisions":["Requires the decennial census questionnaire to include a checkbox or similar option for respondents to indicate the citizenship status of themselves and each household member.","Requires the President's statement to Congress indicating population numbers per state for reapportionment to exclude noncitizens starting with the 2030 census.","Requires the Department of Commerce or Secretary to make publicly available the number of individuals per state disaggregated by citizens and noncitizens.","Includes a severability clause stating that if any provision is found unconstitutional, the remaining provisions will not be affected."],"missing_information":["The exact four detailed categories of citizenship and unlawful residence described in the CRS summary are not present in the reported bill text, which specifically focuses on citizen versus noncitizen categorization.","Specific penalties or enforcement mechanisms for failing to answer the citizenship question on the census questionnaire are not detailed in the provided text."],"plain_summary":"The Equal Representation Act of 2025 changes how the decennial census gathers information and how U.S. House of Representatives seats and electoral votes are distributed among states. It requires the census to collect citizenship status for all household members, mandates that the statement sent to Congress for apportioning representatives exclude noncitizens, and requires public reporting of these statistics.","significance":"This bill alters the method used for congressional apportionment and electoral vote distribution by shifting the basis from total population (all persons) to U.S. citizens only, while introducing mandatory citizenship data collection on the decennial census."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T06:14:05+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr151/BILLS-119hr151rh.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Equal Representation Act of 2025","viability":52.8,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"On a chamber calendar"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage value from the table on the About page.","points":22.75,"value":0.65,"weight":35},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Committee activity","value":"Reported out of committee (or past committee stage)"}],"key":"committee","label":"Committee activity","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Floor activity","value":"Placed on a chamber calendar"}],"key":"floor","label":"Floor consideration","note":"","points":6.0,"value":0.4,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Days since latest action","va